# Coach speech (Korean): the appraisal after the game (src/coach/appraisal.cpp).
# Same keys and variants as assets/coach/speech/en/appraisal.lang (its header documents every placeholder).
#
# Always positive, never blaming. Register: warm polite 해요체; -시- on the player's own actions where a
# teacher uses it (이기셨어요, 잘 두셨어요, 잡으셨어요), never on the coach. The player is never named by a
# pronoun; levels 5-6 may end on a noun (깔끔한 게임., 스테일메이트.).
# Forms from common.lang: a move NUMBER is "{n:moveno}" = "23수째" (spoken "이십삼 수째"), also for
# {crit_no} and {k}; "{moves:move}" = "32수" (a count); "{n:piece}" = "기물 3개"; "{m:time}" = "2번";
# "{pts:point}" = "3점"; "{acc:percent}" = "85%" (spoken "팔십오 퍼센트"), also where English writes a
# bare {acc}; "{n:mistake}" "{m:blunder}" "{n:inaccuracy}"; "{my:obj}" = "제 나이트를". A counted value
# may take a particle ("{n:piece}를", "{acc:percent}였어요"); moves, {eval}, {opening}, {level} and
# {text} never take a sound-dependent one: "{move}, 이 수가 ...", "{crit_move} 대신 {crit_best}".
# Names inserted by {text}, {theme}, {level} (written to fit every sentence that inserts them):
#   appraisal.phase.*   bare nouns, followed only by 에서 or by the noun 단계 ("{text} 단계였어요").
#   appraisal.reason.*  an adverbial phrase that carries its own particle, said right before
#                       무승부 / 비겼어요 ("{text} 무승부예요" = "합의로 무승부예요").
#   theme.*             a nominal -기 phrase, no full stop, always said after a colon.
#   appraisal.level.*   the level name, said in quotes before 레벨 ("“중급자” 레벨").
# The opening name ends the sentence: "{opening:cop}" (시실리안 디펜스예요), "{opening:was}어요" (시실리안
# 디펜스였어요), forms of every family and variation in the openings fragment; or {opening} alone after a colon.
# Terms shared with review.lang: 통과한 폰, 폰의 사각형, 숨 쉴 칸, 무방비, 강제수 (forcing move,
# glossed at level 3 as "체크, 잡기, 위협 같은 강제수").

